  "anchors": {
    "What if your computer could multitask in a heartbeat?": 0.0,
    "How does one CPU let many programs run seemingly at once?": 3.22,
    "Time sharing means the operating system gives each process a tiny slice of CPU time, then moves to the next, repeating in a loop.": 7.24,
    "The code below shows a list of process names and a loop that prints which one runs for each slice.": 14.88,
    "When you run it, you\u2019ll see the CPU jumping from Process A to Process B to Process C over and over.": 20.26,
    "That rapid rotation is what lets many processes use the CPU quickly.": 25.34,
    "Try changing the slice order or adding another process to see the effect.": 30.22
  },
